# GRCh38 silencer training and evaluation datasets

This directory contains two related dataset organizations produced from the
native silencer chromosome distribution:

1. a fixed train/validation/test benchmark for learning curves; and
2. four chromosome-composition outer datasets.

For each chromosome, the usable paired count is the smaller of the available
positive and negative pools. This retains all 202,423 generated negatives and
selects the same number of positives, removing only the 70 positives for which
`genNullSeqs()` did not find a match. No EVN chromosome quotas are imposed.

All positive and negative BED/FASTA pairs remain synchronized by record
position. The selection seed is 42. For negatives, chromosome membership
follows the chromosome-specific source pool recorded in the manifest; the
synthetic null BED coordinate may be elsewhere.

## Fixed learning-curve benchmark

| split | chromosome membership | positive records | negative records | purpose |
|:------|:----------------------|-----------------:|-----------------:|:--------|
| Training 100% | Paired chr3-chr22 and chrX records | 158,088 | 158,088 | Learning-curve model fitting |
| Validation | Paired chr1 records | 29,759 | 29,759 | Early stopping/model selection where supported; validation evaluation otherwise |
| Test | Paired chr2 records | 14,576 | 14,576 | Final evaluation only |
| **Complete benchmark** | chr1-chr22 and chrX | **202,423** | **202,423** | — |

The fixed files are:

```text
train_100_pos.bed
train_100_pos.fa
train_100_neg.bed
train_100_neg.fa
validation_pos.bed
validation_pos.fa
validation_neg.bed
validation_neg.fa
test_pos.bed
test_pos.fa
test_neg.bed
test_neg.fa
train_100_manifest.tsv
train_100_summary.json
```

Validation and test are each written once and are not percentage-subsetted. The
test set must not be used for tuning, early stopping, checkpoint selection, or
threshold selection.

The nested training subsets in `../learning_curves/` are prefixes of one fixed
shuffle of the 158,088-record-per-class training pool:

| training percentage | records per class |
|--------------------:|------------------:|
| 10%  | 15,808 |
| 20%  | 31,617 |
| 40%  | 63,235 |
| 60%  | 94,852 |
| 80%  | 126,470 |
| 100% | 158,088 |

## Chromosome-composition outer datasets

The four groups in `../folds/` partition the fixed training chromosomes. Outer
N omits group N from training. The omitted group is not treated as the final
test set; all four outers use the same fixed chr2 test data defined above.
Counts are per class.

The validation chromosome is chr6 whenever it is present among the included
groups. Outer1 omits the group containing chr6, so it uses chr3 instead.

| outer set | training groups | omitted group | validation chromosome | training records per class | validation records per class |
|:----------|:----------------|:-------------:|:----------------------|---------------------------:|-----------------------------:|
| Outer 1 | 2 + 3 + 4 | 1 | chr3 | 109,656 | 9,728 |
| Outer 2 | 1 + 3 + 4 | 2 | chr6 | 101,655 | 16,642 |
| Outer 3 | 1 + 2 + 4 | 3 | chr6 | 101,753 | 16,642 |
| Outer 4 | 1 + 2 + 3 | 4 | chr6 | 101,546 | 16,642 |

Each `outerN/` directory contains separate `train_{pos,neg}.{bed,fa}` and
`validation_{pos,neg}.{bed,fa}` files. The fixed chr1/chr2 learning-curve
routing remains separate from these outer-specific validation rules.
